# Has anybody tested the model's central assumption? One row per answer, with how many stacks gave
# it.
#
# The most important number here
#   It is the most important number in this repository, and a bare coupling list cannot carry it.
#   This model assumes layers hold their remainders independently. The schema's own annotation says
#   a document with no couplings is not evidence of independence, and an empty list has no column
#   that says whether anybody looked.
#
# What the corpus answers
#   Some stacks file couplings, some say nobody looked, a single-layer stack has no pair to couple,
#   and none says somebody looked and found independence. The central assumption has never been
#   confirmed, and has been contradicted.
#
# Corpus only, and the fixture is why
#   `every-absence.xml` asserts independence on purpose, to show the branch works. Counting a
#   stipulation here would answer "has anybody tested this?" with a yes that nobody earned, and the
#   finding would be false.
-- pm:Stack/pm:couplings/pm:absent, over the corpus.
SELECT CASE
         WHEN s.answer IS NULL              THEN 'somebody looked and the layers move together'
         WHEN s.answer = 'none'             THEN 'somebody looked and found independence'
         WHEN s.answer = 'notApplicable'    THEN 'one layer; no pair to couple'
         ELSE 'nobody looked'
       END AS the_independence_assumption,
       count(*) AS stacks
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) s
JOIN (
    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
) c USING (filing)
GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
